  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "The lead changes hands",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-13-0402-arc-3-tufa-labs-retakes-lead",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs has reclaimed first place in ARC-AGI-3. Its recorded score jumped from 56.52 to 68.91 overnight, taking it past Yi-Chia Chen’s unchanged 67.49. The gap is 1.42 points: a narrow lead after a substantial advance. Chen had taken first in the observed history on October 9 and raised her score twice before this reversal."
    },
    {
      "heading": "NVARC3 breaks up the chasing group",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-13-0402-arc-3-nvarc3-climbs-to-fourth"
      ],
      "text": "NVARC3’s own recorded advance, from 40.97 to 43.94, lifted it from eighth to fourth at the score event. It now sits just 0.30 above the last dance, which is fifth at 43.64. mtg remains third at 45.00. The move changes the order immediately behind the leading pair, though a wide score gap still separates that group from Chen."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The people on the board",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-archive-0",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-archive-0",
        "person-dries-smit-archive-0"
      ],
      "text": "The fresh NVARC3 roster includes Jean-François Puget and Ivan Sorokin, the two credited members of 2025 champion NVARC. Tufa’s ARC-3 roster includes Dries Smit, credited in the 2025 ARC-AGI-3 Preview winning team. Those are useful records of experience; neither a roster nor a score event tells us which person drove this submission or which method produced the gain."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Yesterday’s breakthroughs hold their ground",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-keith-tyser-identity-0",
        "person-keith-tyser-roster-2",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2002-arc-3-arc-slayers-storm-into-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2158-arc-3-arc-slayers-break-into-gold"
      ],
      "text": "ARC Slayers is eighth at 41.19, with Keith Tyser still listed on the roster. Its leap into the top ten was first observed on October 12; the overnight wire revisited that result, but the score has not risen again in this issue’s comparison window. At the other end of the gold group, Lord Han Solo remains eighteenth at 36.98, the final provisional gold score. Public positions remain open to further scoring and the eventual private results."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A competitor opens the door",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2109689542391496948",
        "person-fshindo-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "There is room for a lighter community voice alongside the race. In an October 12 Japanese post, fshindo (@crysis44k) encouraged local LLM enthusiasts who work on harnesses and inference speed to enter competitions, then joked that they might uncover formidable new rivals. That is a friendly invitation, translated here in paraphrase, rather than evidence about any named team’s resources."
    }
  ],
